- heading "Built for GA, not jet brokers." [level=2]
- paragraph: Vref and Aircraft Bluebook focus on larger turbine aircraft. We built the tool that actually works for piston singles, twins, LSA, and experimental aircraft — the planes most pilots actually fly.
- text: / No fabricated sale prices Unlike real estate, GA aircraft sale prices aren't publicly recorded\. We're honest about that — we show asking price ranges with transparent negotiation bands instead of making numbers up\.  Aircraft-specific intelligence Our AI knows the difference between a \d+ Cherokee \d+ and a \d+ SR22T\. Model-specific ADs, known issues, and avionics premiums are all factored in\.  The full buyer workflow Look up the N-number, get the valuation, run the pre-buy checklist, then use flagged issues to negotiate\. One site, the complete process\. How it works/
- heading "From N-number to negotiating position." [level=2]
- text: /\d+ Look up the N-number Enter any US registration and pull the full FAA record — make, model, year, engine, and ownership history in seconds\. \d+ Get the valuation See the typical asking price range for that aircraft, the likely negotiated price, and what's driving value up or down\. \d+ Run the pre-buy checklist Get an AI-generated inspection checklist specific to that make and model\. Mark items pass, flag, or fail\. \d+ Negotiate with confidence Flagged issues feed back into a price adjustment analysis, so you walk in knowing exactly what to ask for\. The toolkit/
